ISO2 ="MAEPQPPSGGLTDEAALSCCSDADPSTKDFLLQQTMLRVKDPKKSLDFYTRVLGMTLIQKCDFPIMKFSLYFLAYEDKNDIPKEKDEKIAWALSRKATLELTHNSDPRGFGHIGIAVPDVYSACKRFEELGVKFVKKPDDGKMKGLAFIQDPDGYWIEILNPNKMATLM"
assert len(CANON)==184 and len(ISO2)==169

# ---------- 1. Observed MS peptides from the EBI Proteins API ----------
cov=np.zeros(185,dtype=int); peps=[]
try:
    r=requests.get("https://www.ebi.ac.uk/proteins/api/proteomics-ptm/Q04760",
                   headers={"Accept":"application/json"},timeout=90)
    if r.status_code!=200:
        r=requests.get("https://www.ebi.ac.uk/proteins/api/proteomics/Q04760",
                       headers={"Accept":"application/json"},timeout=90)
    print("EBI Proteins API status:",r.status_code)
    j=r.json(); j=j[0] if isinstance(j,list) else j
    feats=j.get('features',[])
    print("peptide features returned:",len(feats))
    for f in feats:
        s=int(f['begin']); e=int(f['end']); peps.append((s,e,f.get('peptide',f.get('sequence',''))))
        cov[s:e+1]+=1
except Exception as ex:
    print("EBI proteomics query failed:",ex)

if peps:
    print(f"\nUnique observed peptides: {len(peps)}; residues with >=1 peptide: {(cov[1:]>0).sum()}/184")
    seg=cov[105:120]
    print(f"Coverage over 105-119: min {seg.min()}, max {seg.max()}, residues covered {(seg>0).sum()}/15")
    spanning=[p for p in peps if p[0]<=104 and p[1]>=120]
    print("Peptides spanning residues 104 and 120 in the canonical protein:",len(spanning))
    for s,e,sq in sorted(peps)[:0]: pass
    inseg=sorted({(s,e,sq) for s,e,sq in peps if not(e<105 or s>119)})
    print(f"\nPeptides overlapping 105-119 ({len(inseg)}):")
    for s,e,sq in inseg[:25]: print(f"   {s:4d}-{e:4d}  {sq}")

# ---------- 2. In-silico tryptic digest: isoform-discriminating peptides ----------
def tryptic(seq, missed=1, lo=6, hi=45):
    sites=[0]+[i+1 for i in range(len(seq)-1) if seq[i] in 'KR' and seq[i+1]!='P']+[len(seq)]
    out=set()
    for i in range(len(sites)-1):
        for m in range(missed+1):
            if i+1+m < len(sites):
                p=seq[sites[i]:sites[i+1+m]]
                if lo<=len(p)<=hi: out.add((sites[i]+1,sites[i+1+m],p))
    return out
tc=tryptic(CANON); ti=tryptic(ISO2)
only_c={p[2] for p in tc}-{p[2] for p in ti}
only_i={p[2] for p in ti}-{p[2] for p in tc}
print("\n=== Tryptic peptides unique to the canonical 184-aa protein ===")
for p in sorted(tc,key=lambda x:x[0]):
    if p[2] in only_c: print(f"   {p[0]:4d}-{p[1]:4d}  {p[2]}")
print("=== Tryptic peptides unique to isoform 2 (diagnostic junction peptides) ===")
for p in sorted(ti,key=lambda x:x[0]):
    if p[2] in only_i: print(f"   {p[0]:4d}-{p[1]:4d}  {p[2]}")

# ---------- 3. Figure ----------
